-- title:
--   The disk protocol: kernel learners and adversaries, the canonical law, $\mathbb E_{A,D}[R_T]$, $V_T$, $V_{T,N}$, $D_{\mathrm{sign}}$ and $D_{\mathrm{dir}}$
-- statement:
--   **Protocol.** In round $t$ the learner announces $\rho_t\in\mathcal P(B^2_2)$; the adversary, seeing the public history and $\rho_t$, chooses $g_t\in B^2_2$; then a fresh draw $x_t\sim\rho_t$ is played, with loss $\langle g_t,x_t\rangle$, and $g_t$ is revealed. The public history is $h_t=((\rho_u,g_u,x_u))_{u\le t}\in H_t=(\mathcal P\times B^2_2\times B^2_2)^t$.
--
--   A **learner** is a standard Borel private-state space $S_L$, an initial law $\lambda_L$, and Borel probability kernels $A_t(d\rho,d\tilde s\mid h,s):H_{t-1}\times S_L\to\mathcal P\times S_L$ and $C^L_t(ds'\mid h,\rho,g,x,\tilde s)$. An **adversary** is $S_D$, $\lambda_D$ and kernels $B_t(dg,d\tilde r\mid h,\rho,r):H_{t-1}\times\mathcal P\times S_D\to B^2_2\times S_D$ and $C^D_t(dr'\mid h,\rho,g,x,\tilde r)$; it has no access to the learner's state. The **canonical law** is the unique law obtained from $\lambda_L\otimes\lambda_D$ by drawing, in each round, in this order:
--   $$(\rho_t,\tilde S^L_t)\sim A_t,\quad(g_t,\tilde S^D_t)\sim B_t,\quad x_t\sim\rho_t,\quad S^L_t\sim C^L_t,\quad S^D_t\sim C^D_t .$$
--   $\mathbb E_{A,D}[R_T]$ is the expectation of $R_T$ under it (expectation outside the supremum), and
--   $$V_T=\inf_A\sup_D\mathbb E_{A,D}[R_T],\qquad V_{T,N}=\inf_{A\in\mathcal A_N}\sup_D\mathbb E_{A,D}[R_T],$$
--   where $\mathcal A_N$ is the class of learners whose initial state carries an $N$-tuple $a\in(B^2_2)^N$ (a Borel function of the initial state, possibly random, repetitions allowed; independent of the adversary's initial state) such that against every adversary every played $x_t$ lies in $\{a_1,\dots,a_N\}$ almost surely. The dictionary is **deterministic** when $a$ is a constant.
--
--   **Oblivious adversaries.** $D_{\mathrm{sign}}$ plays $g_t=\varepsilon_te_1$ with fresh independent uniform signs; $D_{\mathrm{dir}}$ draws $\omega$ uniform on $S^1$ (law $\sigma$) once, independently of the learner, and plays $g_t=-\omega$ in every round; the constant adversary plays a fixed $g$.
--
--   This is the model in which every value and every guarantee of the mission is stated.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $\mathcal P(B^2_2)$ is `ProbabilityMeasure Disk` with the Giry $\sigma$-field (generated by $\rho\mapsto\rho(A)$), which equals the Borel $\sigma$-field of the weak topology on the Polish space $B^2_2$. Private states are arbitrary standard Borel types (`S : Type` with `StandardBorelSpace S`). Rounds are 0-based: kernel `prep t` uses the history of the $t$ completed rounds; kernels are given for every `t : ℕ`, those with `t ≥ T` are unused. The law is built by ordered integration (`Measure.bind`) and recorded on `(S_L × S_D) × (Fin t → (ρ, g, x) × S_L × S_D)`: initial states plus, per round, the public triple and both post-round states. `V` and `VN` are real `⨅`/`⨆` over nonempty classes with values in $[0,2T]$. `IsDictLearner T N L` asks for a measurable `dict : L.S → (Fin N → Disk)` with `x_t = dict(S^L_0) i` for some `i`, almost surely, for every adversary and every round; `IsDetDictLearner` asks for a constant tuple. $D_{\mathrm{dir}}$ stores an angle $\theta\sim d\theta/2\pi$ on $[0,2\pi)$ and plays $-(\cos\theta,\sin\theta)$.
-- source:
--   Saravanan, Minimax Realized Full Swap Regret on the Euclidean Disk, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 e7138cc2…), p. 13 (Online protocol, Eqs. (A.1)–(A.3)), pp. 16–17 (Eq. (A.11), Proposition A.5), pp. 19–20 (§A.5), pp. 46, 48 (D_sign, D_dir)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SwapDisk_Main_Regret

/-!
# The disk protocol: kernel learners and adversaries, the canonical law, minimax values

Saravanan, *Minimax Realized Full Swap Regret on the Euclidean Disk*, STOC 2027 submission
(manuscript sha256 e7138cc2…): p. 13 (Online protocol, Eqs. (A.1)–(A.3)), pp. 16–17
(Eq. (A.11), Proposition A.5), pp. 19–20 (§A.5, fixed dictionaries), p. 42 (Appendix D intro).

Conventions.
* `P(B²₂)` is `ProbabilityMeasure Disk` with Mathlib's Giry σ-field (generated by `ρ ↦ ρ(A)`);
  on the Polish space `B²₂` it equals the Borel σ-field of the weak topology used by the paper.
* Rounds are indexed from `0`: round `t` (the paper's round `t + 1`) uses the public history
  `Hist t = (P × K × K)^t` of the `t` completed rounds, a round being `(ρ_u, g_u, x_u)`.
* A learner (adversary) has a standard Borel private-state type `S`, an initial law, a
  preparation kernel and a post-round update kernel per round, with exactly the signatures of
  Eq. (A.11): `A_t : H × S_L → P × S_L`, `C^L_t : H × P × K × K × S_L → S_L`,
  `B_t : H × P × S_D → K × S_D`, `C^D_t : H × P × K × K × S_D → S_D`. The adversary's kernels have
  no learner-state argument. Kernels are given for every `t : ℕ`; those with `t ≥ T` are unused.
* The canonical law (Proposition A.5) is built by ordered integration (`Measure.bind`) in the
  order of Eq. (A.11), starting from `λ_L ⊗ λ_D`: `(ρ_t, S̃^L) ∼ A_t`, `(g_t, S̃^D) ∼ B_t`,
  `x_t ∼ ρ_t` (fresh draw), `S^L_t ∼ C^L_t`, `S^D_t ∼ C^D_t`, the last two independently. It is
  recorded on the trajectory space `Traj = (S_L × S_D) × (Fin t → round × S_L × S_D)`: the
  initial states and, per round, the public triple and both post-round states.
* `E_{A,D}[R_T]` is the Bochner integral of `R_T` (a bounded Borel function of the transcript,
  Proposition A.1) under the canonical law at horizon `T`.
* `V_T = inf_A sup_D E_{A,D}[R_T]` and `V_{T,N}` are real `⨅`/`⨆` over the (nonempty) classes;
  every value lies in `[0, 2T]`, so these are the true infimum and supremum.
* `V_{T,N}`: the learner's initial state carries an `N`-tuple `a = dict(S^L_0) ∈ (B²₂)^N`
  (a Borel function of the initial state, possibly random, repetitions allowed; independent of
  the adversary because initial states have law `λ_L ⊗ λ_D`), and against every adversary every
  played point lies in `{a_1, …, a_N}` almost surely (§A.5). A deterministic dictionary is a
  constant tuple.
-/

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace SwapDisk.Main

/-- `P(B²₂)`: announced probability measures on the disk. -/
abbrev Ann : Type := ProbabilityMeasure Disk

/-- One public round `(ρ_t, g_t, x_t)`: announcement, loss vector, played point. -/
abbrev Round : Type := Ann × Disk × Disk

/-- The public history `H_t = (P × K × K)^t` of `t` completed rounds. -/
abbrev Hist (t : ℕ) : Type := Fin t → Round

/-- An admissible learner (Eq. (A.11)): standard Borel private state, initial law `λ_L`,
preparation kernels `A_t(dρ, ds̃ | h, s)` and post-round update kernels
`C^L_t(ds' | h, ρ, g, x, s̃)`. -/
structure Learner where
  /-- private-state space `S_L` -/
  S : Type
  [mS : MeasurableSpace S]
  [sbS : StandardBorelSpace S]
  /-- initial law `λ_L` -/
  init : Measure S
  [init_prob : IsProbabilityMeasure init]
  /-- preparation kernel `A_t : H_t × S_L → P × S_L` -/
  prep : (t : ℕ) → Kernel (Hist t × S) (Ann × S)
  [prep_markov : ∀ t, IsMarkovKernel (prep t)]
  /-- post-round update kernel `C^L_t : H_t × P × K × K × S_L → S_L` -/
  update : (t : ℕ) → Kernel (Hist t × Ann × Disk × Disk × S) S
  [update_markov : ∀ t, IsMarkovKernel (update t)]

/-- An admissible adversary (Eq. (A.11)): standard Borel private state, initial law `λ_D`,
preparation kernels `B_t(dg, dr̃ | h, ρ, r)` (seeing the public history and the current
announcement, not the learner's state) and post-round update kernels
`C^D_t(dr' | h, ρ, g, x, r̃)`. -/
structure Adversary where
  /-- private-state space `S_D` -/
  S : Type
  [mS : MeasurableSpace S]
  [sbS : StandardBorelSpace S]
  /-- initial law `λ_D` -/
  init : Measure S
  [init_prob : IsProbabilityMeasure init]
  /-- preparation kernel `B_t : H_t × P × S_D → K × S_D` -/
  prep : (t : ℕ) → Kernel (Hist t × Ann × S) (Disk × S)
  [prep_markov : ∀ t, IsMarkovKernel (prep t)]
  /-- post-round update kernel `C^D_t : H_t × P × K × K × S_D → S_D` -/
  update : (t : ℕ) → Kernel (Hist t × Ann × Disk × Disk × S) S
  [update_markov : ∀ t, IsMarkovKernel (update t)]

attribute [instance] Learner.mS Learner.sbS Learner.init_prob Learner.prep_markov
  Learner.update_markov Adversary.mS Adversary.sbS Adversary.init_prob Adversary.prep_markov
  Adversary.update_markov

/-- The trajectory space after `t` rounds: initial states `(S^L_0, S^D_0)` and, for each round,
the public triple `(ρ, g, x)` and the post-round states `(S^L, S^D)`. -/
abbrev Traj (L : Learner) (D : Adversary) (t : ℕ) : Type :=
  (L.S × D.S) × (Fin t → Round × L.S × D.S)

/-- The public history of a trajectory. -/
def Traj.hist {L : Learner} {D : Adversary} {t : ℕ} (z : Traj L D t) : Hist t :=
  fun i => (z.2 i).1

/-- The current private states of a trajectory (the initial states if no round was played). -/
def Traj.cur {L : Learner} {D : Adversary} : {t : ℕ} → Traj L D t → L.S × D.S
  | 0, z => z.1
  | t + 1, z => (z.2 (Fin.last t)).2

/-- The canonical law (Proposition A.5) of the first `t` rounds: ordered integration of the
kernels in the order of Eq. (A.11), starting from `λ_L ⊗ λ_D`. -/
noncomputable def law (L : Learner) (D : Adversary) : (t : ℕ) → Measure (Traj L D t)
  | 0 => (L.init.prod D.init).map (fun p => (p, Fin.elim0))
  | t + 1 => (law L D t).bind (fun z =>
      (L.prep t (z.hist, z.cur.1)).bind (fun ps =>
        (D.prep t (z.hist, ps.1, z.cur.2)).bind (fun gr =>
          (ps.1 : Measure Disk).bind (fun x =>
            ((L.update t (z.hist, ps.1, gr.1, x, ps.2)).prod
                (D.update t (z.hist, ps.1, gr.1, x, gr.2))).map
              (fun sr => (z.1, Fin.snoc (α := fun _ => Round × L.S × D.S) z.2
                ((ps.1, gr.1, x), sr.1, sr.2)))))))

/-- The played points `x_t` of a public history. -/
def Hist.actions {T : ℕ} (h : Hist T) : Fin T → Disk := fun t => (h t).2.2

/-- The loss vectors `g_t` of a public history. -/
def Hist.losses {T : ℕ} (h : Hist T) : Fin T → Disk := fun t => (h t).2.1

/-- The realized full swap regret `R_T` of a public history. -/
noncomputable def Hist.regret {T : ℕ} (h : Hist T) : ℝ := swapRegret h.actions h.losses

/-- `E_{A,D}[R_T]`: the expectation of the realized full swap regret under the canonical law
(expectation outside the hindsight supremum). -/
noncomputable def expectedRegret (T : ℕ) (L : Learner) (D : Adversary) : ℝ :=
  ∫ z, (Traj.hist z).regret ∂(law L D T)

/-- `V_T = inf_A sup_D E_{A,D}[R_T]` (Eq. (A.3)). -/
noncomputable def V (T : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ⨅ L : Learner, ⨆ D : Adversary, expectedRegret T L D

/-- The learner plays in an ex ante dictionary of at most `N` physical points: a Borel
`N`-tuple `dict(S^L_0)` of its initial state (repetitions allowed) contains every played point
almost surely, against every adversary (§A.5). -/
def IsDictLearner (T N : ℕ) (L : Learner) : Prop :=
  ∃ dict : L.S → (Fin N → Disk), Measurable dict ∧
    ∀ D : Adversary, ∀ t : Fin T, ∀ᵐ z ∂(law L D T), ∃ i, (Traj.hist z t).2.2 = dict z.1.1 i

/-- The learner plays in a deterministic ex ante dictionary `a ∈ (B²₂)^N`: every played point
lies in `{a_1, …, a_N}` almost surely, against every adversary. -/
def IsDetDictLearner (T N : ℕ) (L : Learner) : Prop :=
  ∃ a : Fin N → Disk,
    ∀ D : Adversary, ∀ t : Fin T, ∀ᵐ z ∂(law L D T), ∃ i, (Traj.hist z t).2.2 = a i

/-- `V_{T,N}`: the minimax value restricted to learners with an ex ante (possibly privately
randomized) dictionary of at most `N` physical points. -/
noncomputable def VN (T N : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ⨅ L : {L : Learner // IsDictLearner T N L}, ⨆ D : Adversary, expectedRegret T L.1 D

/-- The event `R_T ≤ b` has probability at least `p` under the canonical law. -/
def ProbRegretLE (T : ℕ) (L : Learner) (D : Adversary) (b p : ℝ) : Prop :=
  ENNReal.ofReal p ≤ law L D T {z | (Traj.hist z).regret ≤ b}

/-! ## The oblivious adversaries of Appendix D -/

/-- `e₁ = (1, 0)` as a point of the disk. -/
noncomputable def e1 : Disk := ⟨!₂[1, 0], by simp [disk, EuclideanSpace.norm_eq]⟩

/-- The adversary playing the constant loss vector `g` in every round (trivial state). -/
noncomputable def constAdversary (g : Disk) : Adversary where
  S := Unit
  init := Measure.dirac ()
  prep _ := Kernel.const _ (Measure.dirac (g, ()))
  update _ := Kernel.const _ (Measure.dirac ())

/-- The law of `ε e₁` for a uniform sign `ε`: `(δ_{e₁} + δ_{−e₁}) / 2`. -/
noncomputable def signLaw : Measure Disk :=
  (2 : ENNReal)⁻¹ • Measure.dirac e1 + (2 : ENNReal)⁻¹ • Measure.dirac (negDisk e1)

instance : IsProbabilityMeasure signLaw :=
  ⟨by simp [signLaw, ENNReal.inv_two_add_inv_two]⟩

/-- `D_sign`: independent uniform signs `ε_t`, losses `g_t = ε_t e₁`, generated freshly at each
preparation step, independent of the learner (p. 46). -/
noncomputable def Dsign : Adversary where
  S := Unit
  init := Measure.dirac ()
  prep _ := Kernel.const _ (signLaw.prod (Measure.dirac ()))
  update _ := Kernel.const _ (Measure.dirac ())

/-- `D_dir`: draw an angle `θ` uniformly on `[0, 2π)` as the initial adversary state, i.e.
`ω = (cos θ, sin θ)` uniform on `S¹` (normalized arc measure), independently of all learner
randomness, and play `g_t = −ω` in every round (p. 48). -/
noncomputable def Ddir : Adversary where
  S := ℝ
  init := angleLaw
  prep _ := Kernel.deterministic (fun z => (negDisk (circleDisk z.2.2), z.2.2)) (by fun_prop)
  update _ := Kernel.deterministic (fun z => z.2.2.2.2) (by fun_prop)

end SwapDisk.Main


